n: 3.7.2
name: causes
kind: hub
is: Twelve root causes of complexity and fragility in the old body, ranked by the study by how many recorded failures trace to each and how silent they were; the first four are copies of one meaning, heat changing meaning, kinds read from number ranges and silent recovery. The evidence is mostly dated notes, read and not re-run.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.2.1
name: copies-of-one-meaning
kind: observation
is: A native of the old runtime stood on four mirrors, three kept by hand (manifest row, flt-ops row, serializer arm) and one generated (fkwu-optable.h). The body had two grammars (.fk s-expressions and BML), inside BML two readers (the cursor grammar and the fsc-* statement walker) and, until 2026-10-03, four kernels (C, Go, Rust, TypeScript).
status: observed
src: 2.10.2#81-94 2.10.6#31 2.1.6#407-409 2.10.7#13-16 2.10.1#RC1 2.1#d8c27d222
limit: The page of 2026-10-03 records that for the fourth time in three days a census verdict of 'mint a native' was answered by a routing, for four names (substring, nth-rec, find-loop, str_find); it records an orphaned C arm for str_find only. A unit took the BML route when it carried a 'section [' block, whatever its extension.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.2.2
name: heat-changed-meaning
kind: observation
is: The old runtime's C loop lane inlined a hot callee by argument substitution, so an unread argument lost its effects after 1,024 calls: a plain build landed 3,936 of 780,000 effects. Two machine-code tiers stood at the end, the C loop lane (fk_f64_*) at heat 1,024 and the Form-written page JIT at 4,096; removing the C lane waited at rung R8 of 8.
status: observed
src: 2.1.6#1002-1005 2.10.9#11 2.10.9#16 2.1.6#1276-1278 2.1.6#1381-1384 2.10.11#36-45 2.1.7#557 2.1#270c6f355 2.1#7643c1db4 2.1#80874fd56
limit: Name-bound recipe twins at heat 1,024 were a third tier only from 2026-09-06 (commit 270c6f355) to 2026-09-12 (commit 7643c1db4; the seed's line 557 says the twins left that day). jit-page.bml was first committed on 2026-10-11 (80874fd56), so the twins never stood beside the Form page JIT.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.2.3
name: hot-closure-fault-open
kind: observation
is: A note of 2026-11-24 records a map over a closure holding locals that went wrong at about its 1,024th call in one process; the note says the kernel fault is not repaired and the caller was rewritten as a recursion. The subject line of head commit b8ff978c9 describes that rewrite.
status: observed
src: 2.10.10#11-17 2.1#b8ff978c9
limit: No root cause is recorded. The study read the note and did not reproduce the fault.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.2.4
name: kinds-from-number-ranges
kind: observation
is: The old runtime read a value's kind from ranges of one machine word: any even word an integer, an odd non-negative word a list, strings, floats and functions at large negative bases. eq answered 1 for any two integers at or below -2 until 2026-09-10; (add "abc" 0) answered "abc" until 2026-09-12; (add 9223372036854775807 1) is 0.
status: observed
src: 2.10.6#33 2.10.12#3 2.10.12#11-27 2.10.13#12-28 2.10.14#21-23
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.2.5
name: unresolved-call-became-a-value
kind: observation
is: In the old body an unresolved call was lowered to literal 0 or to pool string 0 and the run continued; one note lists eight shapes of this found from 2026-07-17 to 2026-07-31. In one, 22 JIT bands answered their all-ones masks while hundreds of calls did nothing; in another, fixing one prelude line moved 19 bands to their declared verdicts.
status: observed
src: 2.10.8#11-29
at: 2026-11-24
