n: 3.7.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Six things the study carries forward: nothing kept apart from a value and from a fault, content-addressed nodes under one canonical encoding, control words with undo, one definition per operation over a strict ordered form, the emitter written in the language with live observation, and content-keyed caching moved down to the node.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.8.1
name: nothing-apart-from-fault
kind: finding
is: Keep three outcomes apart from the first day: nothing as axiom 1 defines it, a value, and a text or name that did not parse or resolve. An unbound name is a fault reported with the name when text is bound to nodes, the reader is strict, and a result crossing a boundary is one structured value, never the last line of text plus an exit code.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 1.1 1.5 1.7.19 3.7.2.5 3.7.2.6 3.7.2.11
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.8.2
name: one-canonical-node-encoding
kind: finding
is: Keep content-addressed nodes as the carrier, under one canonical encoding whose hash is the identity and whose bytes are the same in memory and at rest, so a round trip through storage cannot change a node. Interning is the only constructor, a write is atomic, and a shared store reclaims the unreferenced from its first version.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 1.3 3.7.4.1 3.7.2.9
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.8.3
name: control-vocabulary
kind: finding
is: Keep the control vocabulary of choice, fail, cut, stop, try, timeout, store and undo, with a failed option's writes undone by a journal and its finding handed to the next option, and the rule that a retry differs from the attempt before it. These words are the mechanism by which a fault is answered inside the running flow.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.7.4.2 3.7.3.3 1.7.9
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.8.4
name: heat-never-changes-meaning
kind: finding
is: Keep one definition per operation and one strict intermediate form, arguments bound in order before a call, as the single input to interpreter and code generator, with every primitive total over kinds, so heat changes speed and never meaning. A cold-equals-hot check across the heat mark belongs in the bootstrap's own self-test.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.7.4.3 3.7.2.2 3.7.2.3
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.8.5
name: emitter-and-live-observation
kind: finding
is: Keep the emitter written in the language itself, one tier-up mechanism that counts time as well as calls, decline codes that name the missing arm, in-process cells, event-based waiting, and a sampler with a live page as the way performance facts are found. Observation is live signals from the running system, not ledgers committed to the repository.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.7.4.4 3.7.4.7
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.8.6
name: per-node-content-keyed-cache
kind: finding
is: Keep content-keyed stores and byte-reproducible builds, moved down to the node: persisted compiled state keyed by node id, generator id and target; the recipe as the unit of compilation and caching; generated bytes deterministic from the node. A cold run and a warm run then differ only by what hardware bandwidth explains.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.7.4.5 3.7.2.8 1.3
limit: A note of 2026-11-09 records lowering output as not deterministic on one host, because lambda names embedded an allocation-dependent id; the study found no later note saying this was repaired.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: Six things the study lets go, each the cause behind a family of recorded failures: hand-kept second copies of a meaning, coexisting machine-code tiers, kinds and operation identity read from small numbers, recovery of a failure into a value, identity resting on spelling, path or order, and per-incident checks, ledgers and text inside the system.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9.1
name: hand-kept-copies
kind: finding
is: Drop every hand-kept second copy of a meaning: a second grammar or surface that lowers into the first, a second reader, parallel full kernels, and hand-written tables of opcodes, serializer arms or kind tags. A derived table is generated from one declaration at build time or does not exist.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.7.2.1 3.7.4.6
limit: The same study records real faults found only through a second kernel. Whether one small independent conformance reader over the numeric encoding is worth its cost stays unranked by the study.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9.2
name: several-tiers-and-hand-fast-paths
kind: finding
is: Drop coexisting machine-code tiers and hand-written fast paths: at its end the old body ran two tiers with separate thresholds, the C loop lane at heat 1,024 and the Form-written page JIT at 4,096, and a hot call lost effects in the C lane. A fast path is a specialisation the generator derives from the one operation definition, under one tier-up mechanism and one decline vocabulary.
status: inferred
conf: high
src: 2.1.6#1381-1382 2.1.7#557 2.1#7643c1db4 2.1#80874fd56
from: 3.7.2.2 3.7.2.3
limit: The Form JIT did not offer a definition that already wore the C lane's leaf. Recipe twins, a third tier, left the seed on 2026-09-12, before jit-page.bml was first committed on 2026-10-11, so three tiers never stood together with it.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9.3
name: kinds-and-identity-from-small-numbers
kind: finding
is: Drop kinds read from the magnitude or parity of a word, hand-picked small integers as operation identity, numbered modes that multiplex host doors, fixed table sizes in the semantics and behaviour switches. A kind is an explicit, disjoint field; a wrong kind is a named stop or nothing, never a number; integer width and overflow are specified once.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.7.2.4 3.7.2.14
limit: The first-round critic lists the shape of the node id, including whether the kind sits inside it, as not ready to decide. The integer model the owner wants is not stated in anything the study read.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9.4
name: recovery-into-a-value
kind: finding
is: Drop recovery of a failure into a plausible value: an unresolved call lowered to 0, a reader that closes or cuts a source, a harness that exits 0, a check that compares readings with each other only, and a verdict read from the last line of text plus an exit code. A reading that did not arrive is nothing, and an unresolved name is a reported fault.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.7.2.5 3.7.2.6 3.7.2.11 1.1 1.7.19
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9.5
name: identity-by-spelling-path-or-order
kind: finding
is: Drop dependencies and cache keys resting on spelling: load directives in comments, load order, working directory, link-by-name tables, path or mtime keys, whole-closure images. A reference is a node id resolved once when text is read into nodes, every shared artifact carries its maker's identity, and a process-local one ends with its process.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.7.2.7 3.7.2.8 3.7.2.12 1.3
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons

n: 3.7.9.6
name: per-incident-checks-and-text-inside
kind: finding
is: Drop per-incident checks, history ledgers and receipts kept in the repository, text formats and child processes between parts of the system, and single prose pages that hold many claims under one date. Hold a fixed budget of standing checks with a wall-clock ceiling, and treat each proposed new check as evidence of a generic cause to remove.
status: inferred
conf: mid
src: 2.10.5#14
from: 3.7.2.10 3.7.2.11 3.7.2.13
limit: A note of 2026-11-16 records a counter-example: a structural gate caught the return of a removed script, so what a gate catches is read before the gate is removed.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/lessons
